From e1b578583b0dd7cce4b4ff2fa3c998bc28c903bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Junction 2026 team <junction2026@localhost>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:56:41 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 05/13] feat(backend): warn when a dataset records faster than
 its cameras

A dataset samples every camera's latest frame at its own rate, so a camera at
15 fps (or 8) in a 30 fps dataset has each frame recorded twice (or four
times). Loading such a dataset now reports it on the session, naming the
cameras and their rates.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
